    "id": "9ca328069d0d510a9a9e064ec64d7123f1c52dcc",
    "message": "Preserve signed analysis policy with an ordinary CI adapter\n\nIntroduced by: 14595cf8 shared analysis execution by changing two files bound\ninto the published noble-qt693-analysis verification policy.\nUse case: Ordinary static, coverage and CodeQL jobs must keep consuming the\nexisting qualified environment without fabricated replacement evidence.\nReproduction: The six-family compatibility test fails only for the analysis\nfamily, and the real consumer rejects its current qualification-policy digest.\n\nRestore the qualified engine and shell entry point to their approved bytes.\nRoute ordinary static/coverage phases through a separate adapter that imports\nthe unchanged engine's configuration, environment, execution, first-party\nfiltering and cppcheck primitives. Preserve changed-only PR scope, independent\nfailure propagation, coverage transport and the original-checkout ratchet.\n\nThe immutable engine has no phase API, so document partial reuse honestly and\nprotect remaining ordinary orchestration with command-parity tests. Production\nlocks, profiles, signed receipts and their verification are unchanged.\n\nVerification: 47 qualification/adapter tests, 22 profile tests, 33 static\nregressions, 16 executable namespace/failure tests and 11 focused lint tests\npassed. All six production policies match again. CI lint, affected-workflow\nactionlint and whitespace checks passed. The complete integrated quality gate\nwill run before push; remote/native analysis was not executed locally.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>",
